<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish bomb experts search grounded Air France jet.</title>
<headline>Irish bomb experts search grounded Air France jet.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish army bomb disposal experts on Friday started to search an Air France jet which was diverted to Shannon airport after a bomb scare, police said.</p>
<p>The Airbus was taken to an isolated area of the airport, on Ireland's west coast, after being diverted to Shannon on a scheduled flight from Paris to Mexico City.</p>
<p>It was kept under armed guard overnight while its 229 passengers and crew spent the night at a hotel.</p>
<p>The search is expected to take some time, police said.</p>
</text>
